For maximum torque, \[s_{m,T}=\frac{R_{2}}{X_{2}}\] Since \[X_{2}=2\pi fL_{2}\] \[s_{m,T}
=
\frac{R_{2}}{2\pi fL_{2}}\] Hence, \[s_{m,T}\propto \frac{1}{f}\] The synchronous speed is \[N_{s}=\frac{120f}{P}\] Therefore, \[N_{s}\propto f\] Combining the above relations, \[s_{m,T}\propto \frac{1}{N_{s}}\] So, slip for maximum torque is inversely proportional to synchronous speed. \[\boxed{C}\]

