A square pyramid: base perimeter \(= x\), so base side \(= x/4\). Slant height \(= x/2\) (half the perimeter). Lateral surface area \(=\) perimeter of base \(\times\) slant height \(\div 2\): \[LSA = \frac{1}{2} \times x \times \frac{x}{2}
        = \frac{x^{2}}{4}
        = 0.25\,x^{2}\] \[\boxed{\text{D) }0.25\,x^{2}}\] <div class="sol-block sol-keypoints"><div class="sol-block-title">Key points</div><ul><li>Lateral surface area of pyramid \(= \dfrac{1}{2} \times \text{perimeter}
            \times \text{slant height}\).</li></ul></div>
